  "headline": "NAB's cash earnings decreased $11 million or 0.2% to $7,091 million in FY25 from $7,102 million in FY24, broadly stable as the bank reported. Revenue (net operating income) rose 2.9% to $20,813 million, driven by net interest income growth of $644 million (+3.8%), partially offset by a $67 million decline in other operating income. Underlying operating expenses (excluding $130 million of payroll review and remediation charges) increased $305 million or 3.2%. Credit impairment charges rose $105 million to $833 million. Income tax expense increased $27 million. Statutory net profit fell $201 million to $6,759 million, reflecting $303 million of non-cash items (hedging volatility $28m, amortisation $(36)m, acquisition/disposal costs $(295)m) versus $(41)m in FY24.",
